# DAT Registration

## Flow
1. Subscribe to `MetaWearablesDat.registrationStateStream()` BEFORE starting
2. Call `MetaWearablesDat.startRegistration()` — opens Meta AI app
3. User confirms in Meta AI — redirects back via deep link
4. Handle callback: `MetaWearablesDat.handleUrl(uri.toString())`
5. Call `MetaWearablesDat.restartActiveDeviceMonitoring()` after returning from Meta AI (critical on Android)

## RegistrationState
`unavailable(0)`, `available(1)`, `registering(2)`, `registered(3)`

## Disconnect
`MetaWearablesDat.disconnect()` — also opens Meta AI, handle deep link callback the same way.

## Error handling
Catch `PlatformException` with code `REGISTRATION_ERROR`. Details may contain: 0=alreadyRegistered, 1=configurationInvalid, 2=metaAINotInstalled, 3=networkUnavailable.

See `example/lib/providers/device_provider.dart` for canonical pattern.
